Two behaviors worth calling out, both verified against the compiled C:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The uninitialized-buffer reads. [38;5;10mmain[0m leaves the tail of both 1024-byte stack buffers uninitialized, and the library routinely reads past [38;5;10minput_len[0m/[38;5;10mref_len[0m. I modeled the buffers as zero-filled, which is what any input with an explicit NUL terminator depends on. For inputs [3mwithout[23m a terminator the C binary reads live stack junk and its own output changes run to run (ASLR), so no translation can match it.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The [38;5;10mtext_len - pattern_len[0m underflow in [38;5;10mmatch_pattern[0m. When the pattern is longer than the text in the case-sensitive path, the C loop bound wraps to [38;5;10mSIZE_MAX[0m and the scan walks off the buffer. I reproduce it: the scan proceeds through the 1024-byte buffer (so a pattern sitting after an embedded NUL is still found, e.g. [38;5;10m"AB\0XYZ"[0m vs [38;5;10m"XYZ"[0m → 13), and if it runs past the end the program dies from SIGSEGV with no stdout, matching the reference. For short patterns the C binary instead returns a random offset into stack garbage — undefined and unreproducible.[0m[0m
